    "recommendations": "• Trim vegetation along the circular driveway to maintain clear sightlines for responding units approaching and exiting the property.\n• Cut back dense plantings that border the access drive to prevent vegetation from narrowing the usable driving surface.\n• Mark the driveway entrance and exit points with reflective address markers visible from the road at night.\n• Keep a gate or opening in the perimeter fencing at the rear of the property unlocked and accessible for emergency use.\n• Clear a path around the detached structure so responders can reach and move around it without pushing through dense vegetation.\n• Post the property address visibly at the primary driveway entrance so responding units can confirm the correct approach without delay.\n• Identify and communicate to responding units which access point provides the most direct route to the rear of the property."
